lly the case is um  it's a classification issue so  essentially  they allege um that our cryptocurrency  is a security  um we do not um our opinion is also  shared by  many legal experts in the um uh crypto  community um and this is not a unique  question to your token i mean for people  like me who have been following the  space  and follow you know american financial  law as an example  um this this is this is really a big  issue that has significant it's not a  trivial issue  that ultimately uh particularly with the  adoption of bitcoin and other  cryptocurrencies  there's is your belief that at some  point there's going to have to be some  kind of definitive  umbrella ruling as to the handling of  these types of tokens  yeah absolutely because right now the  sec does not give any kind of  adequate guideline to blockchain  companies um  full stop yeah um but  what we're really trying to do um with  you know this whole law students etc is  is work through with the sec to make  sure that  we get things right now and for the  future because  you know um this case has some serious  um implications right for the blockchain  crypto space in the  united states um effectively you know  the industry could be rendered destroyed  over  um if we were to lose the case and it  would apply to  virtually all cryptocurrencies in the  united states how would one  uh get started on odyssey i mean as i  mentioned our  channel is at davidpakman.com  odyssey odysse if you're i mean maybe  tell us both as a user and as a creator  is it just you sign up on the on the web  page  yes so if you're a creator you've got  two options available you can go to the  website odyssey.com that's  um you very kindly spelled it out  odyssey.com  when you sign up there is an option to  sync your entire  youtube library uh which is very helpful  if you're a  creator you don't need to go and  manually upload all of your  videos to a new platform and the other  cool thing about this is whenever you do  upload a new video to youtube it's  automatically going to be  mirrored along with the descriptions for  that video onto odyssey  alternative if you're on iphone you can  get the app from  the app store and just sign up through  there  for users general users it's the same  way you can  either get the app and sign up and watch  content or you can just go to the  website  in terms of moderation um what  is it that is the policy of odyssey in  terms of content because this has been  been a big point of contention  both on the major platforms but also on  some of the new upstart  platforms uh some take the position that  they just allow everything  period and others are saying anything is  allowed  short of something that would be illegal  but then when you say that it becomes  the question of well illegal in what  country different countries have  different frameworks so how do you  approach the moderation  perspective yeah and now um i'll i'll  just pre-face my answer by saying our  current community guidelines are under  revision  but essentially our policies are not  unlike  youtube's in many respects we  we do not allow for copyright content  illegal content child abuse  type content um you know  hate speech of many varieties etc  um i think there is a popular  misconception  um that exists with all these new  alternative platforms that rise up and  that they are free-for-all  uh that is not the case with odyssey in  fact  if we were a free-for-all i don't do i  don't think would last very long to be  is that right  and is that because i mean we saw for  example like parlor ended up having  problems  who's going to host them and amazon web  services said we're not going to host it  but they weren't they weren't so much  legal problems why do you that's  interesting that you've made that  decision  what would it be that prevented you from  lasting too long if you if you were a  free-for-all  it's just like when you are a  free-for-all you end up with  having a platform that's very polarizing  to people  right like um  your product ends up your platform  rather it ends up just appealing to a  niche type of user  so it quickly degrades into something  that  um is not really in alignment with your  original intent  or or purpose that's interesting  so it sounds like it's less about you  think you'd get shut down  but it would it would just limit the  appeal essentially  a hundred percent like we want everybody  to love and use odyssey but if our  platform looks like it's only  um whatever yeah  you know without without you know  calling out any kind of specific  group but if it looks like it's just for  these  you know that's going to be very  polarizing for a lot of people  i think that's a that that's probably  accurate  and interesting that that you uh have  taken that position because not  everybody is uh  taking that position with a lot of these  new platforms you can find  uh the david pakman show on odyssey by  going to davidpakman.com  odyssey that's o-d-y-s-e-e  we've been speaking with julian chandra  who's the chief marketing officer at  odyssey and wals also one of the  platform's creators  uh julian thanks so much to for talking  to us about it today  thanks for having me david appreciate it

